---
layout: landing.njk
permalink: /why/tool/
title: Jenesis - you already wrote the build script
description: The Java build tool that reads your module-info.java as the build. Thirteen common builds, side by side with Maven, Gradle and Bazel, each one built and run.
contact: hello@jenesis.build
contactSubject: Jenesis
docs: /tool/
product: Jenesis
logo: jenesis-tool
repo: https://github.com/jenesis/jenesis
nav:
  - { href: "#examples", label: "Examples" }
  - { href: "#only-what-changed-runs-again", label: "Caching" }
  - { href: "#verify-what-the-build-downloads", label: "Supply chain" }
  - { href: "#two-versions-of-one-library", label: "Layers" }
  - { href: "#start", label: "Get started" }
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{% set bc = buildComparison %}
<div id="top"></div>

<section class="lp-hero">
  <div class="lp-wrap lp-hero__grid">
    <div class="lp-hero__copy">
      <p class="lp-eyebrow">A modern build tool for Java</p>
      <h1>You already wrote <span class="lp-accent">the build script.</span></h1>
      <p class="lp-lede">
        A <code>module-info.java</code> names the module, what it requires and what it exports - Java-native,
        and compiled and checked by <code>javac</code>. Jenesis reads it as the build. <code>java build/jenesis/Make.java</code> compiles, tests and packages the
        project with the JDK you already have - nothing else to write and no plugin to install.
      </p>
      <ul class="lp-pills" aria-label="At a glance">
        <li><strong>Nothing else to write</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Pinned and signed</strong></li>
        <li>Only a JDK</li>
        <li>Reads a <code>pom.xml</code> too</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <figure class="lp-terminal" aria-label="A Jenesis project and its build command">
      <div class="lp-terminal__bar" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
      <pre><code><span class="lp-prompt">$</span> curl -fsSL https://get.jenesis.build | bash
<span class="lp-prompt">$</span> cat sources/module-info.java
<span class="lp-dim">/**
 * @jenesis.release 25
 * @jenesis.main demo.app.Main
 */</span>
module demo.app {
    requires org.slf4j;
    requires com.fasterxml.jackson.databind;
    requires info.picocli;
    requires static org.jspecify;
}
<span class="lp-prompt">$</span> <span class="lp-strong">java build/jenesis/Make.java</span></code></pre>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lp-band lp-band--ink" id="examples" aria-labelledby="examples-title">
  <div class="lp-wrap">
    <p class="lp-eyebrow">Side by side</p>
    <h2 id="examples-title">Thirteen common builds, in four tools.</h2>
    <p class="lp-section-lede">
      Each section below is one build need, written for Jenesis, Maven, Gradle and Bazel. Every file shown was
      built and run with that tool. Where a tool needs a plugin, code by
      hand, or cannot do it at all, the section says so - Jenesis included.
    </p>
    <ul class="lp-legend" aria-label="What the badges mean">
      <li><span class="lp-badge lp-badge--built">{{ bc.statuses.built }}</span> the tool does it</li>
      <li><span class="lp-badge lp-badge--plugin">{{ bc.statuses.plugin }}</span> a plugin or ruleset does it</li>
      <li><span class="lp-badge lp-badge--manual">{{ bc.statuses.manual }}</span> build code you write and keep</li>
      <li><span class="lp-badge lp-badge--none">{{ bc.statuses["none"] }}</span> no way found</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="lp-versions">
      Built and run on Java 25 with
      {% for t in bc.tools %}{{ t.release }}{% if loop.revindex == 2 %} and {% elif not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{% for s in bc.sections %}
<section class="lp-need" id="{{ s.id }}" aria-labelledby="{{ s.id }}-title">
  <div class="lp-wrap lp-need__grid">
    <div class="lp-need__text">
      <p class="lp-eyebrow">{{ loop.index }} of {{ loop.length }}</p>
      <h2 id="{{ s.id }}-title">{{ s.title }}</h2>
      {{ s.lede | safe }}
      <ul class="lp-verdicts" aria-label="How each tool does it">
        {% for t in bc.tools %}{% set e = s.tools[t.key] %}
        <li class="lp-verdict">
          <span class="lp-verdict__who">
            <span class="lp-verdict__tool">{{ t.name }}</span>
            <span class="lp-badge lp-badge--{{ e.status }}">{{ e.badge or bc.statuses[e.status] }}</span>
          </span>
          <span class="lp-verdict__text">{{ e.verdict | safe }}</span>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="lp-tabs lp-tabs--code" data-tabs>
      <div class="lp-tabs__list" role="tablist" aria-label="{{ s.title }}, by tool">
        {% for t in bc.tools %}{% set e = s.tools[t.key] %}
        <button role="tab" id="tab-{{ s.id }}-{{ t.key }}" aria-controls="panel-{{ s.id }}-{{ t.key }}" aria-selected="{{ 'true' if loop.first else 'false' }}"{% if not loop.first %} tabindex="-1"{% endif %}>
{{ t.name }}</button>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% for t in bc.tools %}{% set e = s.tools[t.key] %}
      <div class="lp-tabs__panel" role="tabpanel" id="panel-{{ s.id }}-{{ t.key }}" aria-labelledby="tab-{{ s.id }}-{{ t.key }}"{% if not loop.first %} hidden{% endif %}>
        {% if e.gap %}
        <div class="lp-gap"><p>{{ e.gap | safe }}</p></div>
        {% endif %}
        {% for f in e.files %}
          {% if f.generated or not f.lines %}
          <details class="lp-file lp-file--generated">
            <summary><code>{{ f.path }}</code><span class="lp-file__meta">{% if f.generated %}written by <code>{{ f.generated }}</code>{% else %}{{ f.note }}{% endif %}{% if f.count %} · {{ f.count }} line{{ '' if f.count == 1 else 's' }}{% endif %}</span></summary>
            {% if f.lines %}<pre><code>{% for l in f.lines %}<span class="lp-line{% if l.added %} lp-line--add{% endif %}">{{ l.text }}</span>{% endfor %}</code></pre>{% endif %}
            {% if f.generated and f.note %}<p class="lp-file__note">{{ f.note }}</p>{% endif %}
          </details>
          {% else %}
          <figure class="lp-file">
            <figcaption class="lp-file__head"><code>{{ f.path }}</code><span class="lp-file__meta">{{ f.count }} line{{ '' if f.count == 1 else 's' }}</span></figcaption>
            {% if f.segments %}
            {% for seg in f.segments %}
            {% if seg.folded %}
            <details class="lp-fold">
              <summary>{{ seg.label }}</summary>
              <pre><code>{% for l in seg.lines %}<span class="lp-line">{{ l.text }}</span>{% endfor %}</code></pre>
            </details>
            {% else %}
            <pre class="lp-seg"><code>{% for l in seg.lines %}<span class="lp-line lp-line--own{% if l.added %} lp-line--add{% endif %}">{{ l.text }}</span>{% endfor %}</code></pre>
            {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
            {% else %}
            <pre><code>{% for l in f.lines %}<span class="lp-line{% if l.added %} lp-line--add{% endif %}">{{ l.text }}</span>{% endfor %}</code></pre>
            {% endif %}
            {% if f.note %}<p class="lp-file__note">{{ f.note }}</p>{% endif %}
          </figure>
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
        {% if e.layout %}
        <figure class="lp-file">
          <figcaption class="lp-file__head"><code>Where the sources go</code></figcaption>
          <pre><code>{% for l in e.layout.split("\n") %}<span class="lp-line">{{ l }}</span>{% endfor %}</code></pre>
        </figure>
        {% endif %}
        {% if e.terminal %}
        <figure class="lp-file">
          <figcaption class="lp-file__head"><code>Terminal</code></figcaption>
          <pre><code>{% for l in e.terminal %}{% if l.startsWith("$ ") %}<span class="lp-line"><span class="lp-prompt">$</span> {{ l.slice(2) }}</span>{% else %}<span class="lp-line lp-line--out">{{ l }}</span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</code></pre>
        </figure>
        {% endif %}
        {% if e.commands %}
        <figure class="lp-file">
          <figcaption class="lp-file__head"><code>Commands</code></figcaption>
          <pre><code>{% for l in e.commands.split("\n") %}<span class="lp-line">$ {{ l }}</span>{% endfor %}</code></pre>
        </figure>
        {% endif %}
        {% if e.notes %}
        <div class="lp-notes">
          <p class="lp-notes__title">Worth knowing</p>
          <ul>{% for n in e.notes %}<li>{{ n | safe }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
        </div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {% if s.extra %}{% include "landing-tool/" + s.extra + ".njk" %}{% endif %}
</section>
{% endfor %}

<section class="lp-band lp-band--tint" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-title">
  <div class="lp-wrap">
    <p class="lp-eyebrow">Get started</p>
    <h2 id="start-title">A JDK is all it needs.</h2>
    <p class="lp-section-lede">
      A Jenesis build lives with the project: its engine is plain Java source under <code>build/jenesis/</code>,
      launched by the JDK directly. Installing it is populating that folder.
    </p>
    <div class="lp-tabs" data-tabs>
      <div class="lp-tabs__list" role="tablist" aria-label="How to install">
        <button role="tab" id="tab-curl" aria-controls="panel-curl" aria-selected="true">Install script</button>
        <button role="tab" id="tab-sdkman" aria-controls="panel-sdkman" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">SDKMAN</button>
        <button role="tab" id="tab-brew" aria-controls="panel-brew" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Homebrew</button>
        <button role="tab" id="tab-submodule" aria-controls="panel-submodule" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Git submodule</button>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-tabs__panel" role="tabpanel" id="panel-curl" aria-labelledby="tab-curl">
        <div class="lp-howto">
          <p>From the project root, write <code>build/jenesis/</code> and build.</p>
          <div class="lp-command"><pre><code>curl -fsSL https://get.jenesis.build | bash
java build/jenesis/Make.java</code></pre></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-tabs__panel" role="tabpanel" id="panel-sdkman" aria-labelledby="tab-sdkman" hidden>
        <div class="lp-howto">
          <p>Install once, then initialise each project from the installed copy.</p>
          <div class="lp-command"><pre><code>sdk install jenesis
jenesis-init
java build/jenesis/Make.java</code></pre></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-tabs__panel" role="tabpanel" id="panel-brew" aria-labelledby="tab-brew" hidden>
        <div class="lp-howto">
          <p>Install once, then initialise each project from the installed copy.</p>
          <div class="lp-command"><pre><code>brew install jenesis/tap/jenesis
jenesis-init
java build/jenesis/Make.java</code></pre></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-tabs__panel" role="tabpanel" id="panel-submodule" aria-labelledby="tab-submodule" hidden>
        <div class="lp-howto">
          <p>Pin Jenesis as a git submodule at <code>build/.upstream</code>. A fresh clone plus
            <code>git submodule update --init</code> is then the whole setup, and a new version is a commit you review.</p>
          <div class="lp-command"><pre><code>curl -fsSL https://get.jenesis.build | JENESIS_MODE=submodule bash
git commit -m "Build with Jenesis"
java build/jenesis/Make.java</code></pre></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="lp-after">
      <a class="lp-link" href="{{ docs }}getting-started/">Getting started, step by step &rarr;</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lp-band" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="lp-wrap lp-faq">
    <h2 id="faq-title">Questions</h2>
    <details>
      <summary>Does my project have to use the Java Module System?</summary>
      <p>No. Jenesis reads a <code>pom.xml</code> as the description of what to build, which is the quickest way to
        try it on a project you already have. Where a project declares no modules, its jars resolve by coordinate
        and compile on the class path.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What if a convention does not cover my build?</summary>
      <p>The extension is a small Java function or module describing one step, launched by the JDK like the rest
        of the build - with types, an IDE and refactoring, the same as your application.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How were the examples on this page made?</summary>
      <p>Each one is a project that was built and run with its tool, and the files shown are
        copied from it unchanged. The versions are named under every example.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
